.TH tuldif n 0.3 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuldif
.PP
LDIF (RFC 2849) reader/writer. An entry is an ordered list of {attribute value} pairs (the dn is the "dn" attribute); multi\-valued attributes are repeated pairs. Base64 values (\fBattr:: ...\fR) are decoded via tclutils::tubase64 and re\-encoded on output when a value is not LDIF\-safe.
.SS Commands
.CS
tuldif::parse  ldifText ?-binary attrs?   ;# -> list of entries
tuldif::toLdif entries ?-binary attrs?    ;# -> LDIF text
tuldif::dn         entry           ;# -> dn ("" if none)
tuldif::get        entry attr      ;# -> list of values (nocase)
tuldif::attributes entry           ;# -> attribute names (first-seen order)
tuldif::toDict     entry           ;# -> dict attr -> list of values
.CE
.PP
Continuation lines (a leading space) are unfolded automatically.
.PP
Values are text. RFC 2849 values are UTF\-8, so a base64 value (\fBattr:: ...\fR) is decoded from UTF\-8 after the base64 step, and \fBtoLdif\fR encodes a value to UTF\-8 before base64 (\fBHällo\fR \-> \fBSMOkbGxv\fR). Base64 bytes that are not valid UTF\-8 come back unchanged, one character per byte.
.PP
Binary attributes (0.3): their values are byte strings, one character per byte. \fBparse\fR keeps the decoded bytes (also when they happen to be valid UTF\-8), \fBtoLdif\fR writes them as base64 unchanged; up to 0.2 \fBtoLdif\fR encoded them as UTF\-8 first, so the base64 held other bytes. Binary are \fBjpegPhoto\fR, \fBphoto\fR, \fBaudio\fR, \fBthumbnailPhoto\fR, \fBthumbnailLogo\fR, \fBuserCertificate\fR, \fBcACertificate\fR, \fBcrossCertificatePair\fR, \fBcertificateRevocationList\fR, \fBauthorityRevocationList\fR, \fBdeltaRevocationList\fR, \fBuserSMIMECertificate\fR, \fBuserPKCS12\fR, \fBobjectGUID\fR, \fBobjectSid\fR, \fBmsExchMailboxGuid\fR, every attribute with the option \fB;binary\fR (\fBuserCertificate;binary\fR), and the names given with \fB\-binary\fR. A binary value with a character above \fB\exFF\fR raises \fB{TCLUTILS TULDIF BINARY}\fR.
.PP
Comment lines (\fB#\fR) are not kept.
.PP
\fBtoLdif\fR writes a value as base64 when it is not a SAFE\-STRING: it starts with a space, \fB:\fR or \fB<\fR, ends with a space, or contains a character outside 32..126 (control characters, non\-ASCII).
.PP
Only content records are read. A change record (\fBchangetype: add|modify|...\fR) raises \fB{TCLUTILS TULDIF CHANGETYPE}\fR.
.TS
l l.
Error code	When
\fB{TCLUTILS TULDIF SYNTAX}\fR	a line without \fB:\fR
\fB{TCLUTILS TULDIF CHANGETYPE}\fR	a change record
\fB{TCLUTILS TULDIF BINARY}\fR	\fBtoLdif\fR: a binary value that is not bytes
\fB{TCLUTILS TULDIF OPTION}\fR	an option other than \fB\-binary\fR
.TE
.SS "Additional exported commands"
.PP
Documented for completeness (same module, also covered by the test suite):
.CS
tuldif::addAttr entry attr value               ;# return a copy of an entry with an {attr value} pair appended
tuldif::removeAttr entry index                 ;# return a copy of an entry with the pair at index removed
tuldif::setAttr entry index attr value         ;# return a copy of an entry with the pair at index replaced
.CE
